<p>19 can be expressed as the sum of four perfect cubes:</p>
<p>19 = 33<sup>3</sup> + (-29)<sup>3</sup> + (-25)<sup>3</sup> + 16<sup>3</sup></p>
<p>So can 6941:</p>
<p>6941 = (-3476)<sup>3</sup> + 3090<sup>3</sup> + 2317<sup>3</sup> + 384<sup>3</sup></p>
<p>Can every integer be expressed in this way? It&#8217;s conjectured that the answer is yes, but no one has yet managed to prove it.</p>
